e Minister also: </p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>oversees the <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/ministers/minister-for-the-civil-service\">operation of the Civil Service</a> and government agencies </li>\n  <li>chooses members of the government </li>\n  <li>is the principal government figure in the House of Commons </li>\n</ul>\n","role_payment_type":null,"seniority":1,"whip_organisation":{}},"document_type":"ministerial_role","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2024-07-05T11:32:36Z","schema_name":"role","title":"Prime Minister","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/ministers/prime-minister","withdrawn":false},{"api_path":"/api/content/government/ministers/minister-of-state--198","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/ministers/minister-of-state--198","base_path":"/government/ministers/minister-of-state--198","content_id":"bf5eae5d-1ae8-4032-bbb1-04d10146dfd0","details":{"body":"<p>The Minister’s responsibilities are:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Supporting CDL with coordination of national security policy</li>\n  <li>Resilience </li>\n  <li>Civil contingencies</li>\n  <li>Integrated security fund</li>\n  <li>Investment security</li>\n  <li>Cyber security</li>\n  <li>Government security group, including UK security vetting</li>\n</ul>\n","role_payment_type":null,"seniority":100,"whip_organisation":{}},"document_type":"ministerial_role","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2025-10-06T10:46:25Z","schema_name":"role","title":"Minister of State","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/ministers/minister-of-state--198","withdrawn":false}],"taxons":[{"api_path":"/api/content/environment/water-management","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/environment/water-management","base_path":"/environment/water-management","content_id":"cb4c8377-6fcb-4022-a7a1-98395eb50508","description":"","details":{"internal_name":"Water management (level 2)","notes_for_editors":"","url_override":"","visible_to_departmental_editors":false},"document_type":"taxon","links